      },
      "message": "fix(deburr): start and exit picks for Deburr\n\nThe Deburr takes a start point and an exit point (PickCapability::Chain).\nThe chain nearest the start pick is cut first, from its end nearest the\npick (a closed chain is re-seated at its nearest point). The chain\nnearest the exit pick is cut last, to its end nearest the pick. The cut\ngeometry and the edge breaks stay the automatic ride's; no pick is the\nautomatic ride byte for byte.\n\nRefused by name before any motion: a pick beyond 1.5 tool diameters of\nevery chain, an exit at the start end of an open chain, and a plunge or\nretract column at a moved chain end that comes within the tool radius\nof the part (exact segment-to-facet distance, both moved ends of a\nreversed chain).\n\nRefs #3329\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
